Z||000000||aubicon||08-14-2001||12:57 AM||||the door hinges on my fiero have gone bad the roller on the bottom hinge has shifted so the doors do not opperate properly. im sure that this is a common problem because both of my fieros are falling victim to this. what i am woundering is if you can order the pins and roller to repair the hinges or if you need to order the whole hinge and where would be the best place to get the parts. any help with this would be appriciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||08-14-2001||01:05 AM||||You can get pins & bushings at the Fiero Store and a couple other places. Doni Hagan<BR>had a couple pairs of hinges listed in the mall section. I believe I read he would recondition them if you want. I've bought parts from him before, no problems with anything.<BR>Don<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 2.5<BR>not slow not fast-just halfast||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||08-14-2001||12:54 PM||||The HELP brand blister packs have a set of pins (Chevy S10 pickup) to fit and here's a nice how-to from the Space Coast Fiero Club folks. <A HREF="http://www.castlegate.net/personals/daveheld/TechArt/doorhing.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.castlegate.net/personals/daveheld/TechArt/doorhing.htm</A> <BR>Gary||||reg||1
