Z||000005||Rodney||08-14-2001||04:51 PM||||Quote:<P>what i am wondering is if you can order the pins and roller to repair the hinges <BR>------------------------------------------<BR>I have been looking at the roller part for a few years now. No easy way except having the shafts made via CNC lath and supplying new oilite bushings to replace the nylon bushings used in the OEM steel rollers. The rollers are hardened steel and hold up. It is the bushings that fail. Then the roller sits crooked on the shaft and gets very loose. If it goes too long the roller also eats into the shaft once the bushings are totally worn away. Only fix is to remove the old shaft and replace it with a new one like the one I have looked to have CNC lath made. Cost is high on it if I do make them. I see the Fiero Store offer rebuilt hinges. I wonder what they do with the shaft and roller?? <P>||||reg||1
